WEBVTT

00:04:58.794 --> 00:05:01.255
after an intense series of bombardments

00:05:01.297 --> 00:05:04.508
eventually settle
into an ordered series of planets.

00:05:05.259 --> 00:05:09.096
How often is one
of those planets solid and warm,

00:05:09.138 --> 00:05:11.724
with a water ocean lapping a sandy shore?

00:05:12.683 --> 00:05:15.353
Where do we come from,
and how did we get here?

00:05:17.104 --> 00:05:18.939
The more we learn about exoplanets,

00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:21.650
the easier it is
to target the ones we want.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:25.363
So far, we haven't found any planets
that are like the Earth.

00:05:25.363 --> 00:05:27.239
But I hope we will.

00:05:27.239 --> 00:05:28.991
NASA just spent the last few years

00:05:28.991 --> 00:05:32.578
studying the idea
of a very large telescope in space